{
  "_comment": "Scripted dungeon runs. A run starts when the first player enters a copy of `map` and walks `steps` in order: each step waits for its trigger, then acts. Positions are local to the copy (the instance offset is added). Triggers: enter | cleared:<step id> (every creature that step spawned is dead) | area:<z_below> (a player stands deeper than local z). Actions: spawn (creatures, optional boss_key/template), open / close (gate ids), message (shown to the copy), chest (loot table at a point), complete. D1 adds: trigger hp_below:<step id>:<fraction> (a creature that step spawned is alive below that share of its hit points); a spawn entry may carry `harp` (local point; Fluffy's lullaby pedestal); `entries_per_day` caps new runs per character per server day.",
